  "notes": "The dominant country voice of the 2020s and the fullest realisation of country-trap. The research documents two backbeat classes for this catalogue rather than one, which is why this model authors moods: \"uptempo cuts notated 96–150 with the backbeat on 2&4, and a large group best read as ~68–102 with the snare on beat 3 (half-time) where songdata reports 136–204.\" The `half-time` mood is therefore the only place in this section where `session.halfTime` is true and `snare.placement` is `halftime_3`; the base model and the `riff-first radio` mood keep the straight 2&4 spine. The producer's workflow is documented and two of its parts reach the engine directly: \"tempos deliberately set to odd fractional values\" — so the base mode is 101.5, not 102 — and a riff-first order in which \"guitar layers first, drums added only once the song exists,\" which is why the melody is riff-shaped and the harmony static. The guitar approach is quoted: \"clean electric with no distortion, riff-based rather than solo-based ('less about soloing and shredding, and more about good riffs').\" The 808 takes `counter_riff` because the entry places both layers across the catalogue: \"a tuned 808-style sub is the low end, long and root-locked with slides into chorus downbeats; the ballads substitute a plain electric bass.\" Melody is \"hard-twang baritone with pentatonic runs, cracked notes, pitched-up vocal doubles as texture, and rap-adjacent verse cadences at 4–6 syllables per beat.\" Harmony is held to the three vocabularies the entry names and no others — \"I–V–vi–IV and I–IV–V rendered as two-bar loops, plus i–VI–III–VII on the minor cuts\" — so the `riff-first radio` mood carries only the two major families (mode `progressionFamilies` replaces rather than appends, so anything listed there is a fresh claim, and I–♭VII–IV is documented for Brooks & Dunn, Jay Joyce, Michael Knox and Lainey Wilson in this section, not for Wallen). `session.keys` carries all four minor tonics the entry lists — \"real minor-tonic singles (B minor, E♭ minor, C minor, F minor)\" — alongside the five majors. ⚠ The key concentration around A and F♯ is marked [LOW-CONF] in the research, as is the tempo spine. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the 808 register, the mood weights, the perc densities, the counter ratio and the two mood BPM centres — 122.5 and 85.5 are the midpoints of the two documented bands, a derivation rather than a quoted figure; only the bounds themselves are the research's.",
